{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790282728,"nonce":"VKdbR5sFnVnE0RMfpm31KQ1T5ok=","title":"ZYNTAX_LOWER_FORCE_FALLBACK=1 panics a Python program at finalize: can't resolve symbol zb_hook_instance_type","message":"With ZYNTAX_LOWER_FORCE_FALLBACK=1 set, zypy (8844ca79, ZYPY_LLVM=1) runs a small program such as\n\n    def double(x): return x * 2\n    print(list(map(double, [1, 2, 3])))\n\nprints the first line and then the warm-up thread panics in cranelift-jit backend.rs: can't resolve symbol zb_hook_instance_type. The forced path sets wanted to None and calls adopt_all_prelowered, but some library hook the program defines is left unresolved. The switch exists to bisect the reach-driven lowering, so it should produce the same program as the reach-driven path. Found while verifying R-reachability-lowering; present on the base binary, not caused by it.","files":null}]}